{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"loony-fabric-bunny","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nEven after runtime routing moves to registries, manual consumers can recreate drift: `scripts/gen_cli_reference.py` regex-parses the intercept ladder and owns a curated command table; help/exit-code tests rebuild route sets; clean-wheel CI does not exercise every approved help and lazy-reference contract.\n\n## Approach\nMake the route/help and capability registries the enumerable inputs for documentation and contract checks.\n\n- Generate `docs/cli-reference.md` from canonical routes and committed package-help bytes, including compatibility/hidden status without maintaining `INTERCEPT_COMMANDS` or regex-parsing source.\n- Replace manual route unions in overview, help, argparse, and exit-code conformance tests with registry enumeration.\n- Keep package-data help authoritative; generation embeds bytes and metadata but never synthesizes usage text.\n- Extend the existing local-capable optionality harness and `.github/workflows/_optionality.yml` clean-wheel lane to install a no-extras wheel, run every top-level help form in a fresh directory, assert no store/config/handler/heavy import, and exercise lean contrast modes.\n- Add a full-runtime-extra contract that resolves every lazy handler/selector and validates every capability-to-extra reference without executing commands. This belongs in the full-extra lane rather than normal startup.\n- Smoke-test `rebar-mcp` separately. Every check has a repository command usable without GitHub Actions; CI invokes the same commands.\n\nRegistry validation covers resource census and retired-token collisions at runtime. The full-extra contract covers string-reference typos that normal lazy startup intentionally cannot detect. No source-text grep substitutes for observable help/dispatch contracts.\n\n## Compatibility and Rollback\nDuring expansion, retain old exported census names as values derived from the registry so external/string-patch test sites receive the same sets. Reference output changes only where S2 intentionally added canonical help and grouped discovery. Reverting the generator/tests/CI restores the former checks without changing runtime or stored data.\n\n## Testing\nUse generator byte-checks, real wheel subprocesses, import blockers, and full-extra symbol resolution. Prove each exact test is collected and executes in a gating local/CI command. Negative fixtures include a missing handler symbol, unknown selector, stray help resource, omitted route, hidden alias leakage, retired token, and heavy optional import.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `scripts/gen_cli_reference.py --check` derives the complete reference from registry/resource enumeration with no regex intercept scan or hand-maintained command-description census.\n- [ ] Overview/help/exit-code coverage tests enumerate canonical, compatibility, hidden, and retired route classes from the registry rather than reconstructing policy sets.\n- [ ] A clean no-extras wheel renders every approved top-level help form in a fresh directory with exact bytes and no config/store/handler/heavy-import effect.\n- [ ] The full-extra contract resolves every handler/selector reference and every capability-to-packaging-extra mapping without executing command logic.\n- [ ] The same repository commands run locally and in CI, and `rebar-mcp` receives a separate entrypoint smoke test rather than a synthetic CLI verb.","id":"6755-d43c-b962-45a8","parent_id":"09ae-e827-1cac-452d","priority":1,"tags":["rp05","cli"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"RP-05 S5 — Derive CLI reference and distribution contracts from the registries"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787069641619693001,"uuid":"aecda70d-c857-42f9-89fa-39ee70907b26"}